//! The `row-rule-break` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the
//! behavior for breaking row rules into segments where row rules intersect column gaps.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - intersection: Row rules always break when they intersect column gaps, with row rule segments
//! starting and ending at container and gap edges.
//! - none: There are no breaks in row rules when they intersect column gaps; rather, a continuous
//! row rule is painted the whole width of the container, from edge to edge.
//! - normal: In grid, flex containers, and multi-col layout, behaves as `none`. This is the default
//! value.
//!
//! Grammar: none | normal | intersection
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-gaps-1/#propdef-row-rule-break
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/row-rule-break
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

